## Animate one element

Give any tag `anim=zoom`, `delay=0.2`, `dur=0.7` and it comes in that way.
Together with `<step>` it is a build, like PowerPoint's entrance effects:

<step>
  <text anim=fade>
    Fades in on the first click, no movement.
  </text>
</step>

<step>
  <text anim=zoom dur=0.7>
    Zooms in from a smaller size.
  </text>
</step>

<step>
  <text anim=pop out=4>
    Pops with a little overshoot, then leaves again on the fourth click.
  </text>
</step>

<notes>
  anim: fade | rise (default) | zoom | left | right | down | blur | pop | none. delay and dur are seconds; at=N sets the click, out=N the click where it disappears. A step passes its attributes to everything inside.
</notes>
